, it applies to a claim of its person's grade on that date in place of the sheet's; blank: none, the sheet's applies), the pot (shared out among the members of each balanced pool by their shares; blank: none; not dated), the parent sheet (a grade with no rate in force on a date here takes the parent's, then its parent's, up to three levels up; blank: none; not dated), the fiscal year start month (1 to 12; blank: 1; not dated), the alert threshold (a person whose due-total goes above it is alerted in the audit; blank: off; not dated), the rounding mode (half-up or half-even: a claim with one in force on its date rounds every live figure by it; blank: none, the policy date decides), the default grade (a person added by the quick-add bar, or by an import line with a blank grade, gets it; changing it changes no one; blank: A; not dated), each grade's clerk limit (on the sheet's today, it applies to a claim of its person's grade then in place of the sheet's; blank: none, the sheet's applies), the score thresholds, mid and high (whole numbers: while both are set, each person shows a band; blank: none; not dated), and the form that sets them. A clerk settles a claim only when its due is at or below the
